From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:03:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Gather block collision boxes without allocating

World.getCubes returned a List<AxisAlignedBB>, so every solid block in an
entity's swept volume cost a 64-byte box plus the list. Those boxes were
built inside Block.getCollisionBoundingBox - a megamorphic call - so
neither C2 nor Graal could scalar-replace them, and the cost grew
linearly with the number of blocks scanned.

Collision boxes are now appended to a CollisionBoxSink as six raw doubles
each. The sink is a reusable per-thread buffer; callers take a mark(),
fill it, read the region back, and reset(mark), so nested queries (the
step-up trial in Entity.move runs while the main pass's boxes are still
live) stack safely instead of needing a second buffer.

Block gains getCollisionBounds(world, pos, state, double[] out) as the
single source of truth for a block's shape; the 36 blocks that overrode
getCollisionBoundingBox now override that instead, and the 12 multi-box
blocks (stairs, fences, panes, ...) override addCollisionBoxes the way
they used to override addCollisionBoxesToList. getCollisionBoundingBox
remains for the cold callers that genuinely want an object (item
placement, arrow impact, block-update checks) and just wraps the scalar
form.

Callers that only asked "is anything in the way?" now use
World.hasCubes(entity, six doubles), which needs no list at all.

Verified: full test suite passes; server boots on JDK 25 and ticks 30s
with no exceptions or movement warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
index 9402ff3895887160253cabc59d087c71044a6ace..87d2d5b7a4beafd70a91f31e8c8521a64b4bdfb6 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
@@ -290,9 +290,40 @@ public class Block {
 
     }
 
+    // Athena start - scalar collision shape.
+    //
+    // getCollisionBounds is the single source of truth for a block's collision box: it writes the
+    // six bounds into the caller's array and says whether the block has a box at all. The old
+    // getCollisionBoundingBox is kept for the cold callers that genuinely want an object (item
+    // placement, arrow impact, block-update checks) and simply wraps it.
+    //
+    // addCollisionBoxes is the gathering entry point used by World.getCubes; blocks made of several
+    // boxes (stairs, fences, ...) override it the way they used to override addCollisionBoxesToList.
+    public boolean getCollisionBounds(World world, BlockPosition blockposition, IBlockData iblockdata, double[] out) {
+        out[0] = (double) blockposition.getX() + this.minX;
+        out[1] = (double) blockposition.getY() + this.minY;
+        out[2] = (double) blockposition.getZ() + this.minZ;
+        out[3] = (double) blockposition.getX() + this.maxX;
+        out[4] = (double) blockposition.getY() + this.maxY;
+        out[5] = (double) blockposition.getZ() + this.maxZ;
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    public void addCollisionBoxes(World world, BlockPosition blockposition, IBlockData iblockdata,
+                                  double qMinX, double qMinY, double qMinZ, double qMaxX, double qMaxY, double qMaxZ,
+                                  CollisionBoxSink sink, Entity entity) {
+        double[] out = sink.scratch();
+
+        if (this.getCollisionBounds(world, blockposition, iblockdata, out)) {
+            sink.addIfIntersects(out[0], out[1], out[2], out[3], out[4], out[5], qMinX, qMinY, qMinZ, qMaxX, qMaxY, qMaxZ);
+        }
+    }
+
     public AxisAlignedBB getCollisionBoundingBox(World world, BlockPosition blockposition, IBlockData iblockdata) {
-        return new AxisAlignedBB((double) blockposition.getX() + this.minX, (double) blockposition.getY() + this.minY, (double) blockposition.getZ() + this.minZ, (double) blockposition.getX() + this.maxX, (double) blockposition.getY() + this.maxY, (double) blockposition.getZ() + this.maxZ);
+        double[] out = new double[6]; // cold path only
+        return this.getCollisionBounds(world, blockposition, iblockdata, out) ? new AxisAlignedBB(out[0], out[1], out[2], out[3], out[4], out[5]) : null;
     }
+    // Athena end
 
     public boolean isOpaqueCube() {
         return true;
